{"amendments":[{"body":"Strengthen `probe_thermal_suppression` so the cool control must itself reproduce. In `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:572-576`, the test falls back to `warm_readiness <= cool_readiness` whenever both arms finish with zero juveniles, and the only control-arm check in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:611-624` covers health, not breeding. A regression that suppresses spawning or hatching in both tanks can still pass as long as the warm arm is slightly worse and drops one clutch. Add a positive-control assertion on the cool arm (juveniles, hatch events, berried cycles, or a minimum readiness floor) so this probe actually verifies thermal suppression relative to a working breeding baseline.","rationale":"Without a positive cool-arm breeding assertion, a global reproduction regression can slip through this scenario undetected."},{"body":"Make the summary run emit structured traces on successful executions instead of keeping them in memory only. `enable_probe_instrumentation()` attaches `SimTracer::new(Verbosity::Trace)` with no sink in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:103-107`, and `HarnessRun::finish()` returns immediately for successful non-verbose runs in `crates/tank_harness/src/lib.rs:649-656`. In practice `all_shrimp_probes_summary` prints the population summary but does not log any trace output unless callers remember `TANK_E2E_VERBOSE=1`. Persist a JSONL sink or write the trace bundle from the summary path unconditionally.","rationale":"The task explicitly called for an e2e runner that logs structured traces; the current happy-path behavior loses that output."},{"body":"Extend the persisted checkpoint/trace payloads so failures include per-tick, per-stage shrimp diagnostics instead of only aggregate shrimp fields. The only per-stage formatter is the ad hoc `shrimp_diag()` string in `crates/tank_harness/tests/e2e_shrimp_scenario_probes.rs:136-171`, but `TankSnapshot` checkpoints only serialize aggregate shrimp fields in `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs:58-66`, and the tracer records aggregate condition/reserve rather than per-stage condition/reserve in `crates/tank_core/src/tracing.rs:315-368`. That means a failing artifact cannot reconstruct the requested adult/sub-adult/juvenile condition and reserve state for each tick. Add explicit per-stage fields to the snapshot, tracer, or a shrimp-specific failure attachment written by `HarnessRun::finish()`.","rationale":"These probes are meant to support calibration and failure diagnosis; aggregate-only artifacts are not enough to explain why a scenario drifted."}],"summary":"I ran the shrimp scenario probe suite and it passes, but I found three substantive gaps: the thermal suppression test can pass even if the cool control never breeds, the summary runner does not actually emit structured traces on successful runs, and the persisted artifacts still do not contain the per-stage per-tick shrimp diagnostics that the scenario deliverable depends on."}